  "scope": "Explicit opt-in; existing default admission, Fast, pipelines, allocator, selectors and ABI unchanged.",
  "algorithm": [
    "Existing escape, overlap, byte-splat, observer, debug and initialized-on-all-path proofs are shared. No capture contracts or speculative memory operations added.",
    "Field discovery uses a set; overlap checks are grouped by slot. Escaped slots do not spend the field or overlap-analysis budget. Pathological slots are skipped without rejecting later small objects.",
    "Large mode prunes SSA parameters by backward live-in propagation from loads before local definitions. The original must-initialization proof still runs before mutation.",
    "Analysis exhaustion leaves the current field untouched and retains already completed promotions. Every syntactic edge, including duplicate destinations, receives the needed argument. Unreachable blocks and entry backedges still reject the function."
